    <ol class="cases">
        <li class="case">
            <div class="case-meta">
                <p class="case-number">01</p>
                <p class="case-kind">API Architecture</p>
                <h2>Reverse-Engineering Global Ticketing APIs</h2>
                <ul class="case-tags">
                    <li>Legacy APIs</li>
                    <li>Data Mapping</li>
                    <li>Technical Specs</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="case-body">
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="case-label">The Challenge</h3>
                        <p>A global ticketing platform needed its legacy, multi-layered event data integrated into our CDP. Documentation was fragmented, and venues and events were related in ways the structure did not make obvious.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="case-label">My Solution</h3>
                        <p>I manually mapped the API logic, reverse-engineering the data relationships. I designed the JSON transformation schema and guided Engineering on the exact implementation path, so their whole event catalogue could be standardised at once.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="case-outcome">
                        <h3 class="case-label">The Outcome</h3>
                        <p>Real-time segmentation across their full event history, with the legacy dependency still intact.</p>
                    </div>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="case">
            <div class="case-meta">
                <p class="case-number">02</p>
                <p class="case-kind">Complex Integration</p>
                <h2>Sports League Bi-Directional Sync</h2>
                <ul class="case-tags">
                    <li>Bi-Directional Sync</li>
                    <li>CRM Architecture</li>
                    <li>Multi-Tenant</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="case-body">
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="case-label">The Challenge</h3>
                        <p>Onboarding a multi-tenant sports league of 10+ clubs, each running its own tools and changing them without notice. They required a bi-directional sync between B2B CRMs, mobile apps, and gamification platforms. We had to handle conflicting data edits and push segmented audiences back to their CRM.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="case-label">My Solution</h3>
                        <p>Designed which system wins each field when two sources disagree, and the two-way sync that applies it. I coordinated the integration across Ticketing, E-commerce, and Membership systems.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="case-outcome">
                        <h3 class="case-label">The Outcome</h3>
                        <p>Clubs could push targeted segments from the CDP back into their own CRM and sell against them.</p>
                    </div>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="case">
            <div class="case-meta">
                <p class="case-number">03</p>
                <p class="case-kind">Data Privacy</p>
                <h2>US Sports League: Protecting Minors' Data</h2>
                <ul class="case-tags">
                    <li>Minors' Privacy</li>
                    <li>Data Modeling</li>
                    <li>Identity Resolution</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="case-body">
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="case-label">The Challenge</h3>
                        <p>A US professional sports league with a nationwide youth club network, and rigid data lake pipelines, needed to onboard its entire under-18 membership base. Under strict legal constraints, marketing had to reach parents and guardians without exposing any minor's personal data.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="case-label">My Solution</h3>
                        <p>Led the technical discovery with their data engineers and structured their data sources with them. I designed the account's identity resolution and a "Parent/Guardian" entity model in the CDP that routed all communications to authorised adults while keeping the non-adult profile data siloed for analysis only.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="case-outcome">
                        <h3 class="case-label">The Outcome</h3>
                        <p>The model was signed off by the client's own data-protection and engineering teams and shipped, letting them reach the guardian audience without minors' personal data leaving the analytics silo.</p>
                    </div>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="case">
            <div class="case-meta">
                <p class="case-number">04</p>
                <p class="case-kind">AI Automation</p>
                <h2>Segmentation Engine Migration</h2>
                <ul class="case-tags">
                    <li>Generative AI</li>
                    <li>REST APIs</li>
                    <li>SQL</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="case-body">
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="case-label">The Challenge</h3>
                        <p>Every customer account had to move from an old segmentation engine to a new one, with every segment rebuilt rule by rule. Done by hand it was slow, repetitive work, and the larger the account the worse it got.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="case-label">My Solution</h3>
                        <p>I built an AI toolkit backed by a knowledge library of how the platform is configured. It reads the SQL behind the existing segments, triages what needs recreating, bootstraps the new engine and rebuilds the rules and segments through the portal's API.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="case-outcome">
                        <h3 class="case-label">The Outcome</h3>
                        <p>A migration now needs only a planning phase; the toolkit does the rebuild. The same toolkit now builds dashboards and analytics tables from a customer's raw data sources.</p>
                    </div>
